From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:29:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Keep bionic malloc, pthread_attr and properties on arm guests

An arm guest on a 64-bit host cannot take host pointers or host
records: a glibc heap pointer or a host prop_info pointer lies above
4 GiB and does not fit the guest pointer, and glibc pthread_attr_t is
56 bytes where bionic arm has 24. Drop the native_bridge_malloc*
family, android_mallopt, pthread_attr_* and __system_property* from
the arm stub list and leave malloc_init.cpp and the no-op
__libc_init_scudo.cpp out of the arm build, so bionic own malloc
dispatch, scudo init, pthread_attr_* and system properties (which lose
to the stubs only under -z muldefs) define them. Scudo and the
property area map through the emulator, which places non-fixed guest
mappings below 4 GiB; the area file is the one the host reads.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [NBS arm assumes a 32-bit host, where host heap pointers, host prop_info pointers and pthread_attr_t fit the guest]
Patch-Reason: the stub list and sources are compiled into the guest libc; no launcher, loader or environment setting can remove a stub definition that overrides bionic under -z muldefs
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 android_api/libc/Android.bp    |   8 +++
 android_api/libc/stubs_arm.cpp | 102 ---------------------------------
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 102 deletions(-)

diff --git a/android_api/libc/Android.bp b/android_api/libc/Android.bp
index 4045b904b89c525fcea64370d497d0668d82581b..c53d783fa3ec1af13baa789108ae12922f37fc45 100644
--- a/android_api/libc/Android.bp
+++ b/android_api/libc/Android.bp
@@ -72,6 +72,14 @@ cc_library {
                 ":libc_sources_shared_arm",
                 "stubs_arm.cpp",
             ],
+            // A 32-bit guest on a 64-bit host keeps bionic's own allocator
+            // (scudo, mapped through the emulator below 4 GiB) and its own
+            // pthread_attr_*: a host heap pointer or a host pthread_attr_t
+            // does not fit the guest's 32-bit words.
+            exclude_srcs: [
+                "__libc_init_scudo.cpp",
+                "malloc_init.cpp",
+            ],
 
             cflags: [
                 "-DCRT_LEGACY_WORKAROUND",
